{
 "encounter_id": "00619",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good morning, doctor. Thank you for seeing me. I'm back about my rash, though it is much improved, I must say."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good morning. Lovely to hear. Remind me where it began, because I see you were away. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, we went to Goa for a week and my back and chest came out in tiny red spots, very prickly and itchy."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And how are those spots now, compared to when you came to me first?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Mostly gone from the chest. The itching has gone away from my back too, thank God. It is only my neck now that is still red."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "So the chest rash has settled, the itch on the back has settled, and the neck is still active?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Exactly so. The neck is still a bit itchy, especially at night when I'm warm under the blanket."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And any new blisters, or skin breaking down or weeping?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, no blisters at all. Nothing weeping either."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Wonderful. Now, tell me which creams you are using, so I can check them. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I am using hydrocortisone cream 1% twice a day on the neck, calamine lotion when it itches, and also cetirizine 10 mg at night."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Cetirizine at night helps with itching. Are you allergic to any medicines, or have you ever been?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, I have no known allergies. None at all."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you. Your medical history, anything long-term that I should know?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I have type 2 diabetes, and I take tablets for it. Also asthma since childhood, but it is quiet nowadays."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Noted. Any operations in the past?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Gallbladder removal, in 2017. Done by keyhole, very neat."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Let me look at your skin. Please turn around and lift your shirt. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Of course, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 78, blood pressure 130 over 82, temperature 36.7, oxygen 98 percent, respiratory rate 16.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "These are good numbers, no? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Very good. Back and chest are clear now, just faint marks. The neck has a patch of red pinpoint spots.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It looks worse when I look in the mirror than it feels. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Heat rash usually looks dramatic. This looks like it is settling, and I would call it heat rash that is clearing, with some irritation on top of it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it contagious? My daughter is worried. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not at all. Keep the neck cool and loosely covered, cotton collars, no tight chains or scarves."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I have been wearing my gold chain, I will remove it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please do. Continue the hydrocortisone on the neck for another five days, then stop."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Another five days. Good. And the cetirizine? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take it at night until the itching has gone, then you may stop. I would like to see you again in two weeks to make sure it has gone."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "In two weeks. I will book on the way out. Thank you, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "My pleasure. Keep cool, and enjoy the rest of the monsoon. ~"
  }
 ],
